## 1. File register (and the write allowlist)

| file | lines | allowlist entry |
|---|---|---|
| `godot/src/ui/Hud.tscn` | 13 | "a scene that mounts it (Hud.tscn)" |
| `godot/src/ui/Hud.gd` | 1125 | "godot/src/ui/Hud.gd" |
| `godot/src/ui/ViewState.gd` | 728 | "a view-model it needs (src/ui/ViewState.gd)" |
| `godot/tests/ui/hud_audit.gd` | 1013 | "an audit test" |
| `docs/implementation/ui-recreation/evidence/uir-08-hud-audit.log` | this file | evidence |

Not created, deliberately:
* `godot/tests/ui/hud_audit.tscn` — the allowlist permits it; it is not needed. A second,
  script-less mount would duplicate what UIR-24's capture harness does with real data, and a
  script-less HUD renders an empty frame by design (see §8, "honesty"). The audit mounts
  `Hud.tscn` itself.
* No edit to any file outside the five above. `git status --short` in this repo shows the whole
  `docs/implementation/ui-recreation/`, `godot/src/ui/`, `godot/tests/ui/` and `godot/assets/ui/`
  trees as untracked (the lane's own state); no commit, no push, no deletion was made.

Nothing was mounted into the router (`godot/src/ui/ScreenRouter.gd` is untouched) and no
integration-owned file was modified: `ScreenShell.*`, `screens/ScreenContract.gd`,
`focus/UiFocusBridge.gd`, `data/UiData.gd`, `UiStrings.gd`, `theme/*`, `godot/game/hud.gd`,
`godot/game/match_controller.gd` and `godot/tests/ui/{router,data,theme_probe}*` are exactly as
this wave found them.

