| `ScorePanel` | (32,30) 413.84x95 | anchor (0,0), offsets 32/30, min 414x95 | content-driven height ~120 (theme roles are larger than the reference's compact 9px/22px pair); width grows only if a localised chip is wider than 414 |
| `ActionsRow` | (963.48,30) 284.52x54 | anchor (1,0), right inset 32, top 30, height 54, min width 284.52 | inner min is 290 (110 timer + 4x42 buttons + 3x4 gaps): 5.5 px wider than measured |
| `ModeStrip` | not in the probe (mode HUD is a separate capture state) | (32, 196) 414x96, below the scoreboard, `visible` only while a mode view is set | prototype decision, documented as such |
| `MiniMapPanel` | `.mini-map` top 100 / right 16, padding 6, canvas 86x122 | anchor (1,0), right inset 16, top 100, 98x150 | height = 122 + 2x6 pad + 14 label + 4 gap (measured padding/gap used) |
| `ServeBanner` | `#serveBanner` centred (markup 493-495) | anchor (0.2..0.8, 0.5), ±34 px, `HudPauseCard` box | prototype decision for a fixed frame; the reference centres the same element |
| `MatchPanel` | panel state: 1068x217, 16 px screen insets, **below the canvas** (y 796 on a 720 px canvas) | anchor bottom, insets 16, bottom offset 54 (= 16 + 28 toggle + 10 gap) | the reference's panel is off-frame; the prototype puts it in-frame at the same side insets and above the feed toggle. Height ~125 because the reference's 217 includes the 12-row control legend, which is UIR-13's (`control_rows()` is the empty seat) |
| `MatchFeed` | immersive: fixed left 24 / bottom 20, toggle 28 tall; panel state: 1068x28 row at 16 px insets | anchor bottom, left 24 / bottom 20 when the panel is closed, inset 16 when open; band = 28 collapsed, +130 when the log is expanded | none on the anchors; the log's own row styling is a theme gap (§7) |

Region count is 7 and `panels()` returns them in tree order:
`ScorePanel, ActionsRow, ModeStrip, MiniMapPanel, ServeBanner, MatchPanel, MatchFeed`.

Overlap arbitration (the one state the reference never had to resolve, because its panel sits
below the canvas): opening the command panel collapses the event log, because the measured
