## 5. Field mapping (live adapter — no fabricated stats)

`ViewState.from_state(state, meta)` reads the runner's own `SimState`
(`godot/src/sim/state.gd`) and returns exactly the 44 keys in `ViewState.FIELDS`. The audit
asserts that equality, and maps each field against the reference formula:

| HUD field | state source | reference | rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| `player_score`/`ai_score` | `playerScore`/`aiScore` | `js/ui.js:1276-1287` | as-is |
| `player_name`/`ai_name` | `athlete.id`, `ai.id` (+ `pvpAthlete` for pvp) | `js/ui.js:1279-1295` | `athlete_<id>_name`, last word only |
| `match_info` | `mode`, `humanMode`, `sets`, `games`, `tieBreakPoints`, `pointsToWin`, `tieBreak` | `js/ui.js:1300-1316` | tournament/career label + season + round, then `quick`/`ptsToWin`/`setLbl`/`tieBreak`/`tieBreakShort`/`gamesLbl` |
| `active_label_*` | `activePlayerKey`, `serving`, `ball.serveInFlight`, `activePlayerAuto`, `paddle.y` | `js/ui.js:1318-1330` | `manual`/`autoSwitchLbl` flag, then serve/receive/role/locked, side from `netY` |
| `tactic_*` | `playerTeamTactic`, `tacticFlashUp`/`Down`, `activePlayerKey` | `js/ui.js:1332-1340` | queued tactic, or the movement override while flash is set |
| `combo_*` | `combo` | `js/ui.js:1342-1350` | `combo` string + the four-colour ladder + glow from combo 3 |
| `timer_text` | `elapsed` | `js/ui.js:1290-1298` | `MM:SS` with `floor` (not `round`) |
| `special_*` | `specialReady`, `specialCooldown` | `js/ui.js:1320-1326` | `clampf(0..1)`, dim while on cooldown |
| `shot_*` | `shotIntent`, `shotRead.advice`/`profile`/`active`/`eta`/`perfectWindow`, `shotCharge`, `shotAim` | `js/ui.js:1356-1368` | `power = shotCharge`, `aim = 50 + shotAim*42`, `timing = 52 - eta*72` clamped to -8..108, window `perfectWindow*155` clamped to 5..17 |
| `serve_*` | `serving`, `pointPause`, `pointMessage`, `serveSide`, `serveAttempts` | `js/ui.js:1360-1368` | point-pause beats serving; `serveFirst`/`serveSecond`/`serveOpp` |
| `log_lines` | `events` | `js/game.js:3344` ring | newest first, at most five, each id resolved to a sentence |
| `map_points` | four paddles + `ball` | `js/main.js:1397-1428` | canvas 108x154 with an 11 px pad, court 80..880 x 56..564, net from `Frozen.court().netY` |

The HUD paints every one of those: the audit compares `report()["texts"]` against the view for
all text-bearing fields (§9), so a view-model that computed but never painted fails.

`report()["view"]` is the model's own output (`_view.duplicate(true)`), never a re-serialisation
of the painted labels — the audit can tell a fabrication from a measurement.

