## 8. Static verification performed in this wave (no Godot)

Tooling: `gdtoolkit` (pip, into `/tmp`) provides `gdparse`/`gdlint`; it parses GDScript without
running a project.

```
gdparse godot/src/ui/Hud.gd            -> no output (parses)
gdparse godot/src/ui/ViewState.gd      -> no output (parses)
gdparse godot/tests/ui/hud_audit.gd    -> no output (parses)
gdlint  <the three files>              -> only max-line-length / max-file-lines findings,
                                          the same class the repo's own audits report
```

Additional static sweeps run this wave (ad-hoc Python, same rules the audit applies at runtime):

* every literal locale key in the three files exists in `locale_data.gd` — 0 misses;
* every `theme_type_variation` named exists in `padel_theme.tres` — 0 misses;
* every `_palette("…")` key exists in the theme's `Palette` — 0 misses;
* the prose-literal rule (strip `#` comments, exempt developer-marker lines, flag any remaining
  literal containing a space) over `Hud.gd`, `ViewState.gd`, `Hud.tscn` — **0 offenders**, with a
  non-vacuity probe of the same rule (1/1 flagged on a synthetic source). The audit re-runs this
  rule in-project (`hud/no_user_facing_literal_lives_in_the_huds_own_files` and
  `hud/the_scene_declares_no_prose_of_its_own`, probed by
  `hud/the_literal_scan_flags_prose_in_a_synthetic_source`);
* zero `add_theme_stylebox_override` / `add_theme_font_size_override` / literal `Color(` outside
  comments in the two sources — the audit asserts this as
  `hud/no_node_carries_a_colour_or_a_stylebox_of_its_own`.

Honesty of the empty frame: before the first `refresh()`, every field is blank, the meters sit
at zero, the markers are hidden and the banner is off — the HUD never shows a plausible 0-0 it
was not given. The audit asserts this as six `hud/before_the_first_refresh_*` checks.

